7. [Date of Receipt or Acceptance] Each Contracting Party may, at its discretion, determine under what circumstances documents actually submitted to, or fees actually paid to, the following bodies or addresses shall be considered as received or accepted by its trademark office:  
(1) a branch or regional office of the trademark office;  
(2) where the Contracting Party is an intergovernmental organization referred to in Article 26(1)(ii) of the Treaty, the trademark office of a State representing that Contracting Party;  
(3) an official postal service;  
(4) a postal or delivery service or agency designated by the Contracting Party;  
(5) an address other than that designated by the trademark office.

IV. [Exceptions Provided in Article 14(3) of the Treaty]  
The exceptions provided in Article 14(3) of the Treaty refer to situations where the following time limits have not been observed:  
(1) the time limit for taking remedial measures granted under Article 14(2) of the Treaty;  
(2) the time limit for submitting a request for remedial measures under Article 14 of the Treaty;  
(3) the time limit for payment of renewal fees;  
(4) the time limit for taking action before the appeal board or other review body within the trademark authority;  
(5) the time limit for actions between parties in a proceeding;  
(6) the time limit for submitting the declaration referred to in Article 3(1)(a)(vii) or the declaration referred to in Article 3(1)(a)(viii) of the Treaty;  
(7) the time limit for submitting a declaration, in accordance with the law of the Contracting Party, for determining a new filing date for a pending application; and  
(8) the time limit for making amendments or additions to a claim of priority.

