4. When this Convention comes into force or at the time it comes into force:

(a) In the case of a Member which has ratified the Minimum Age (Industry) Convention (Revised), 1937, and which assumes the obligations of this Convention and has specified a minimum age not less than fifteen years in accordance with Article 2 of this Convention, such ratification shall ipso jure involve the immediate denunciation of that Convention;

(b) In respect of non-industrial employment as covered by the Minimum Age (Non-Industrial Employment) Convention, 1932, if a Member which has ratified that Convention assumes the obligations of this Convention, such ratification shall ipso jure involve the immediate denunciation of that Convention;

(c) In respect of non-industrial employment as covered by the Minimum Age (Non-Industrial Employment) Convention (Revised), 1937, if a Member which has ratified that Convention assumes the obligations of this Convention and has specified a minimum age not less than fifteen years in accordance with Article 2 of this Convention, such ratification shall ipso jure involve the immediate denunciation of that Convention;

(d) In respect of maritime employment, if a Member which has ratified the Minimum Age (Sea) Convention, 1936, assumes the obligations of this Convention and has specified a minimum age not less than fifteen years in accordance with Article 2 of this Convention or has specified, pursuant to Article 3 of this Convention, that this Convention applies to maritime employment, such ratification shall ipso jure involve the immediate denunciation of that Convention;

(e) In respect of employment in sea fishing, if a Member which has ratified the Minimum Age (Fishermen) Convention, 1959, assumes the obligations of this Convention and has specified a minimum age not less than fifteen years in accordance with Article 2 of this Convention or has specified, pursuant to Article 3 of this Convention, that this Convention applies to employment in sea fishing, such ratification shall ipso jure involve the immediate denunciation of that Convention;

(f) In the case of a Member which has ratified the Minimum Age (Underground Work) Convention, 1965, and which assumes the obligations of this Convention and has specified a minimum age not less than that prescribed by that Convention in accordance with Article 2 of this Convention or has specified, pursuant to Article 3 of this Convention, that this age applies to underground employment, such ratification shall ipso jure involve the immediate denunciation of that Convention.

5. Upon the entry into force of this Convention or at the time it enters into force:

(a) With respect to the Minimum Age (Industry) Convention, 1919, the assumption of obligations under this Convention shall entail the denunciation of that Convention in accordance with Article 12 thereof;

(b) With respect to agriculture, the assumption of obligations under this Convention shall entail the denunciation of the Minimum Age (Agriculture) Convention, 1921, in accordance with Article 9 thereof;

(c) With respect to maritime employment, the assumption of obligations under this Convention shall entail the denunciation of the Minimum Age (Sea) Convention, 1920, in accordance with Article 10 thereof, and the Minimum Age (Trimmers and Stokers) Convention, 1921, in accordance with Article 12 thereof.
